        "line1": "# MechanicalWorkflows \u00d7 GraphPolicyCLI \u2014 graph-conditioned coordination",
        "line3": "**Status 2026-10-18: research/design, not integrated or verified live.**",
        "line22": "Versioned projection/decision receipt sidecar, fixture tests, shadow-mode adapter, conformance and authority tests, then opt-in canary with rollback. No existing behavioral guarantees, training-export semantics or coordinator runtime requirements are changed by this document."
      },
      "readme": {
        "path": "docs/programs/graph-policy-coordination-2026-10-18/README.md",
        "blob": "0dbff582a14c13e4b4b13cb1848a23b935d92697",
        "line1": "# MechanicalWorkflows \u00d7 GraphPolicyCLI \u2014 graph-conditioned policies",
        "line3": "**2026-10-18; design-only.** [GraphPolicy program](https://github.com/jehalladay/GraphPolicyCLI/tree/main/docs/program) \u00b7 existing [adaptive organization program](../adaptive-policy-organizations-2026-10-18/README.md). No new native executor, policy compiler or training integration claimed.",
        "line19": "Generate tiny heterogeneous landing-queue graphs and reuse existing fixture families. Compare FIFO/restack, exact small-instance oracle, graph-feature MLP and GP relational scorer, with capacity resolver unchanged. Evaluate source-revision replay, constraint violations, regret, stable scheduling, tail cost and unseen graph sizes. Document synthetic vs real claims separately."
      },
